RULE NUMBER
023

TITLE
Forge: Seed the Component GUIDE.md and Regenerate the Reference

ROLE
You are the Planton Code Partner working inside the developer's local workspace in Cursor. This rule seeds the newly forged component's authored wisdom layer -- its `GUIDE.md` -- from what THIS forging session just learned, then regenerates the catalog reference so the new kind's generated pages exist and link the guide. You have just read the provider's documentation, designed the spec, and written the IaC module: you currently know more about this component's judgment calls than any later session will.

SCOPE
- Creates `catalog/<provider>/<kindfolder>/<version>/GUIDE.md`
- Runs `make generate-reference` (whole-catalog; writes the new kind's `reference.md`, the guide head link, and the updated indexes)
- Does not modify any other existing files

PREREQUISITES
- The component's spec, IaC module, docs, hack manifest, and presets exist (rules 001-022 complete)
- `_rules/docs/write-planton-component-guide.mdc` -- the authoring standard this rule follows

SEQUENTIAL STEPS

1) **Collect the session's judgment**
   Before it evaporates, list what this forging session learned that the schema cannot carry:
   - Internal conventions the component participates in (state ownership, flags whose
     semantics have consequences, components that supersede inline conveniences)
   - Judgment calls made while designing the spec (why a field is a reference, why a
     default is what it is) -- ONLY where a composer's decision depends on them
   - Diagram impact: what this component renders as, and what choices hide or reveal
     infrastructure on the architecture diagram
   - What it pairs with (from the foreign keys just declared) and what well-known name
     it substitutes for, if any

2) **Filter by the five laws**
   Apply `_rules/docs/write-planton-component-guide.mdc` -- especially: no general cloud
   knowledge, judgment framing with consequences, every claim grounded in the files this
   session just wrote. If honest filtering leaves almost nothing, write the short guide
   that remains -- never pad. A three-paragraph guide that changes decisions is success.

3) **Write the guide**
   Create `GUIDE.md` beside the component's protos following the write rule's shape.

4) **Regenerate the reference**
   Run `make generate-reference`. This materializes the new kind's `reference.md`
   (with the `**Guide**:` head link), the provider index row (Example and Guide
   columns), the root index counts, and the graph edges -- the freshness gate fails
   the tree if this step is skipped.

5) **Self-validate**
   - `go test ./pkg/explain/refgen/` passes (drift gate + wisdom guardrails: embedded
     manifests validate, links resolve, placement correct)
   - The new `reference.md` head carries the Guide link

OUTPUT
- The guide's path and a one-line summary of the judgment it carries
- Confirmation that the reference regeneration ran and the gates pass

SUCCESS
- `GUIDE.md` exists beside the component's protos and follows the write rule
- `make generate-reference` run; drift gate and wisdom guardrails green
- No general-knowledge filler; every claim grounded in this session's own artifacts

NOTES
- This rule is part of the forge sequence (step 21 in the orchestrator)
- The guide is a LIVING document: it will be extended as adoption feedback arrives;
  seeding it now preserves knowledge that only exists during the forging session
- Check whether the provider's catalog is settled before investing heavily in guide
  content -- wisdom authored against a catalog under active rework will be wrong
  before it is read; in that case seed only what is structural and certain
